      "message": "This is one option - to define pipeline stage flags independent of the backends that can then be translated into `VkShaderStageFlags`, Dawn\u0027s `ShaderStage`, etc.\n\nThe other option would be to handle this entirely internally to each backend that cares about descriptor organization. That could look like defining a `VulkanDescriptorData` struct that contains `DescriptorData` and the `VkShaderStageFlags` directly, for example.\n\nAs it stands now, though, Dawn and Vulkan use the same general shader stage visibilities for the same descriptors (aka Dawn `entries`). If that holds true going forward (which I would think it would?), it may make more sense to say \"Uniforms at `UniformSlot::kPaint` have pipeline shader stage flags of `PipelineStageFlags::kFragmentShader` at the graphite level and have each backend translate that as appropriate.\n\nI could also see an argument for equating that at the graphite level being overkill or unnecessary, though. LMKWYT.",
